cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use swiftsnp, please cite it as below, and also cite snp-dists, from which it derives."
title: "swiftsnp: a byte-identical drop-in replacement for snp-dists"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-20
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/joe-b-christensen/swiftsnp"
authors:
  - family-names: Christensen
    given-names: Joe
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-0908-1299"
    email: joechristensen@clin.au.dk
    affiliation: "Translational Neuropsychiatry Unit (TNU), Department of Clinical Medicine, Aarhus University, Denmark"
keywords:
  - SNP distance matrix
  - genomic epidemiology
  - snp-dists
  - performance
abstract: >-
  swiftsnp computes pairwise SNP distance matrices from FASTA alignments with output byte-identical to
  snp-dists 1.2.0 (-j 1) for every option and thread count. On five published alignments it was 336x faster
  than the fastest other tool that writes the same matrix, and 2,894x faster than single-threaded snp-dists
  (geometric means, two threads, AVX-512 CPU).
references:
  - type: software
    title: "snp-dists: pairwise SNP distance matrix from a FASTA sequence alignment"
    version: 1.2.0
    authors:
      - family-names: Seemann
        given-names: Torsten
      - family-names: Klötzl
        given-names: Fabian
      - family-names: Page
        given-names: Andrew J.
    repository-code: "https://github.com/tseemann/snp-dists"
    license: GPL-3.0-only
